WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:03.440
The biggest drop in this video comes at fourteen seconds.

00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:05.820
Now you know which part to fix.

00:00:08.179 --> 00:00:10.679
Here's what Markdrop shows after you share a link.

00:00:12.039 --> 00:00:17.619
Analytics covers every link you own: views, people, watch time, and how many read to the end.

00:00:18.193 --> 00:00:20.093
Worth a look points out what stands out.

00:00:22.355 --> 00:00:26.975
For a document, see how far people read, section by section, and where they leave.

00:00:27.570 --> 00:00:29.350
You see which code blocks get copied.

00:00:29.890 --> 00:00:31.350
What they copy is never stored.

00:00:33.674 --> 00:00:38.094
For a PDF, see which pages people reach, and where the biggest drop is.

00:00:40.754 --> 00:00:44.494
For video, a curve shows who's still watching, second by second.

00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:49.290
You see what gets rewatched or skipped, and whether it played well, phones included.

00:00:51.546 --> 00:00:55.766
Each version keeps its own numbers, so you can tell if a new cut works better.

00:00:58.013 --> 00:01:02.613
Audience shows where views came from, and how often a chat app showed a preview of your link.

00:01:05.063 --> 00:01:09.343
Live shows who's on your links right now, by country and device, and nothing more.

00:01:11.794 --> 00:01:15.914
Signed in, your own visits don't count, and your team's are left out by default.

00:01:16.646 --> 00:01:18.846
IP addresses are kept only as a hash.

00:01:19.646 --> 00:01:20.726
Patterns, never people.

00:01:23.106 --> 00:01:26.357
Analytics come with your account, at markdrop.in.
